1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:01,881
Hi, I'm Sohan.

2
00:00:01,881 --> 00:00:05,161
This is an equipment inspection app I built in Power Apps Canvas,

3
00:00:05,161 --> 00:00:07,061
on Dataverse.

4
00:00:07,324 --> 00:00:10,044
It's one of two builds of the same app,

5
00:00:10,044 --> 00:00:13,544
made to find exactly where Canvas stops.

6
00:00:13,938 --> 00:00:18,538
Inspectors check forklifts and conveyors across three warehouse sites.

7
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:22,020
They need a checklist that changes with each answer,

8
00:00:22,020 --> 00:00:25,940
a live risk score, and photos of any defect.

9
00:00:26,211 --> 00:00:28,111
The home screen lists every inspection,

10
00:00:28,111 --> 00:00:30,921
with its status and its risk.

11
00:00:31,186 --> 00:00:33,866
Four of these twelve are high or critical,

12
00:00:33,866 --> 00:00:36,606
so the problems stand out straight away.

13
00:00:38,426 --> 00:00:42,046
A new inspection starts with the site, then the equipment.

14
00:00:43,643 --> 00:00:46,023
This forklift is high criticality,

15
00:00:46,023 --> 00:00:49,383
so every risk point counts one and a half times.

16
00:00:53,136 --> 00:00:55,936
The checklist is a tree stored in Dataverse,

17
00:00:55,936 --> 00:00:57,916
and it grows as you answer.

18
00:00:58,177 --> 00:01:02,037
This forklift is out of service, with damage in the hydraulics,

19
00:01:02,037 --> 00:01:04,517
and fluid is leaking.

20
00:01:04,786 --> 00:01:07,126
No spill kit has been deployed.

21
00:01:07,126 --> 00:01:11,926
That's level five, and the score is fifty-two point five, high.

22
00:01:12,206 --> 00:01:13,926
The next question is at level six,

23
00:01:13,926 --> 00:01:16,656
and it's a critical safety stop.

24
00:01:16,909 --> 00:01:18,569
It never appears.

25
00:01:18,569 --> 00:01:21,669
Power Fx functions can't call themselves,

26
00:01:21,669 --> 00:01:26,029
so there's one formula per level, and the app stops at five.

27
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:30,520
Change the first answer to yes, and the whole branch closes.

28
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:32,110
Its points go with it.

29
00:01:32,365 --> 00:01:35,205
Now the operator has no valid licence.

30
00:01:35,205 --> 00:01:37,485
Forty-five points would only be medium,

31
00:01:37,485 --> 00:01:40,275
but a critical stop forces the top band.

32
00:01:44,035 --> 00:01:48,615
Inspectors can add a photo, and mark the defect with the pen.

33
00:01:48,867 --> 00:01:52,447
It's freehand only, and the strokes save apart from the photo.

34
00:01:52,447 --> 00:01:54,417
That's another limit I measured.

35
00:01:57,212 --> 00:01:58,512
Review lists every answer,

36
00:01:58,512 --> 00:02:00,952
and shows how the score was worked out.

37
00:02:01,219 --> 00:02:03,839
Submit saves it to Dataverse,

38
00:02:03,839 --> 00:02:07,109
and the new inspection goes straight to the top of the list.

39
00:02:09,631 --> 00:02:13,011
Under the hood it's six Dataverse tables, five screens,

40
00:02:13,011 --> 00:02:17,531
and over three and a half thousand lines of Power Fx source.

41
00:02:17,791 --> 00:02:20,851
Twenty-three Playwright tests drive the published app,

42
00:02:20,851 --> 00:02:23,981
and check what it saved in Dataverse.

43
00:02:24,243 --> 00:02:28,223
All of this is sample data, in a developer environment.

44
00:02:28,495 --> 00:02:30,035
The next build moves the checklist

45
00:02:30,035 --> 00:02:33,255
and the photo markup into code components.

46
00:02:33,506 --> 00:02:36,566
The full build, the tests and the scripts are on my GitHub,

47
00:02:36,566 --> 00:02:40,436
and there's more on my portfolio. Thanks for watching.
